{"name":"Celeste","hex":"#b2ffff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Celeste","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from French [in turn from Latin].","A minor city in Hunt County, Texas, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Celeste"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mount Celeste","blocks":[{"text":"Mount Celeste is the unofficial name for a mountain located on Vancouver Island, British Columbia. It shares the name Celeste with two peaks in the Cariboo region of the BC Interior. Within the boundaries of Strathcona Provincial Park, this peak lies at the north end of Rees Ridge. Iceberg Peak lies at the south end of this ridge."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Celeste","wikidata":"Q6920089"},{"title":"Celeste, Texas","blocks":[{"text":"Celeste is a city in Hunt County, in the U.S. state of Texas. The population was 809 at the 2020 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Celeste_November_2015_1_%28U.S._Route_69%29.jpg/330px-Celeste_November_2015_1_%28U.S._Route_69%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celeste%2C_Texas","wikidata":"Q975056"},{"title":"Celeste (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Celeste is a 2018 platform video game developed and published by indie studio Maddy Makes Games. The player controls the player character Madeline, a young woman with anxiety and depression, who endeavors to climb Celeste Mountain, a fictional version of Mount Celeste. During her climb, she encounters several characters, including a personification of her self-doubt nicknamed \"Badeline\", who attempts to stop her from reaching the mountain's summit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Celeste_box_art_full.png/330px-Celeste_box_art_full.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celeste_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q28451532"},{"title":"Celeste (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Celeste or Céleste is a given name or surname which derives from the Latin caelestis, meaning heavenly or celestial."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celeste_(name)","wikidata":"Q56292311"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Celeste_summit.png/500px-Celeste_summit.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Celeste_summit.png/1280px-Celeste_summit.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Celeste_summit.png/500px-Celeste_summit.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mount Celeste as depicted in Celeste","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeleste_summit.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Celeste%2C_Texas_%28ca._1905-1909%29.jpg/500px-Celeste%2C_Texas_%28ca._1905-1909%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Celeste%2C_Texas_%28ca._1905-1909%29.jpg/500px-Celeste%2C_Texas_%28ca._1905-1909%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sanger Street (circa 1905–09)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeleste%2C_Texas_(ca._1905-1909).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Celeste_screenshot_02.png/500px-Celeste_screenshot_02.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Celeste_screenshot_02.png/1280px-Celeste_screenshot_02.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Celeste_screenshot_02.png/5